    "title_eng": "5.2 AMS / ATMS: Process Hierarchy & Task Tree Governance",
    "content_eng": "# 5.2 ActivityTaskManager (ATMS) & WindowManager: Task Stack & Process Hierarchy\n### Android Systems & Bionic Architecture Handbook — Module 5: Lecture 2\n\n**Course Series:** AOSF-HB-2026-SYS-MOD5-02  \n**Author:** Eunho Kim (@uno-km), AMEVA Systems Architecture & Research Engineering Group  \n**Target Architecture:** Android ActivityTaskManagerService (ATMS)  \n**Curriculum Scope:** Multi-Window Hierarchy, Task & Activity Records, Launch Modes, Lifecycle Transitions  \n**Compliance Standard:** Apache-2.0 / OpenSSF Best Practices / CNCF Neutrality Guidelines  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Abstract & Architectural Formulation\n\nIn modern mobile environments, user interaction spans single tasks, split-screen multi-window displays, picture-in-picture (PiP), and external desktop displays (Samsung DeX).\n\nManaging this spatial and chronological complexity is the responsibility of the **ActivityTaskManagerService (ATMS)** (bifurcated from legacy AMS in Android 10). ATMS maintains a tree hierarchy of displays, task stacks, and activity records, translating user intent into deterministic lifecycle callbacks (`onCreate`, `onResume`, `onPause`, `onStop`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Interactive WASM Systems Engineering Lab (Colab-Style Cells)\n\n### [Cell 1~3] Python Task Stack & Launch Mode Simulator\n```python\n# [Colab Cell 1: Environment & Task Stack Setup]\nimport sys\n\nprint(\"=== [Cell 1: ATMS Task Stack Model Initialized] ===\")\nprint(\"Python Architecture:\", sys.version.split()[0])\n\n# [Colab Cell 2: Android Activity Launch Mode Simulator]\nclass ActivityStackSimulator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.stack = []\n\n    def launch_standard(self, activity_name):\n        self.stack.append(activity_name)\n\n    def launch_single_top(self, activity_name):\n        if self.stack and self.stack[-1] == activity_name:\n            print(f\"  [singleTop] {activity_name} already top! Invoking onNewIntent()\")\n        else:\n            self.stack.append(activity_name)\n\n    def launch_single_task(self, activity_name):\n        if activity_name in self.stack:\n            idx = self.stack.index(activity_name)\n            popped = self.stack[idx+1:]\n            self.stack = self.stack[:idx+1]\n            print(f\"  [singleTask] Found {activity_name}! Popped above: {popped}\")\n        else:\n            self.stack.append(activity_name)\n\n# [Colab Cell 3: Verification & Execution Benchmark]\nsim = ActivityStackSimulator()\nsim.launch_standard(\"MainActivity\")\nsim.launch_standard(\"DetailActivity\")\nsim.launch_single_top(\"DetailActivity\")\nsim.launch_single_task(\"MainActivity\")\n\nprint(f\"\nFinal Task Stack State: {sim.stack}\")\nassert sim.stack == [\"MainActivity\"], \"singleTask must leave MainActivity at root\"\nprint(\"Status: 100% Deterministic LaunchMode Resolution PASS\")\n```\n\n### [POSIX Shell] Task Hierarchy & Window Stack Probe\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -eu\necho \"=== [Android ActivityTaskManager Task Hierarchy Probe] ===\"\necho \"Timestamp: $(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC')\"\n\nif command -v dumpsys >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    dumpsys activity activities | head -n 15\nelse\n    echo \"  [Sandbox Mode] Virtual ATMS Hierarchy:\"\n    echo \"  Display #0 (Default Display: 1080x2400)\"\n    echo \"    RootTask #1 (Type: Standard, Bounds: [0,0][1080,2400])\"\n    echo \"      Task #45 (Affinity: com.android.launcher3)\"\n    echo \"        ActivityRecord: LauncherHomeActivity (Resumed: TRUE)\"\nfi\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. ATMS Window & Task Spatial Hierarchy\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Root[\"RootWindowContainer (Global Display Arbiter)\"]\n    Root --> D0[\"DisplayContent (Display #0: Internal Display)\"]\n    Root --> D1[\"DisplayContent (Display #1: External HDMI / DeX)\"]\n    D0 --> RT1[\"TaskDisplayArea (Standard Window Space)\"]\n    RT1 --> T1[\"Task (ID 101: Browser Task)\"]\n    RT1 --> T2[\"Task (ID 102: Split-Screen Task)\"]\n    T1 --> AR1[\"ActivityRecord (Tab 1: WebViewer)\"]\n    T1 --> AR2[\"ActivityRecord (Tab 2: CheckoutPage)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Launch Modes & Intent Flags Deconstructed\n- **`standard`**: Spawns a new `ActivityRecord` and pushes it atop the target task stack unconditionally.\n- **`singleTop`**: If the target activity is already at the top of the stack, reuses the instance by dispatching `onNewIntent()` rather than creating a new instance.\n- **`singleTask`**: Routes to an existing task with matching affinity, popping all activities above it off the stack (CLEAR_TOP behavior).\n- **`singleInstance`**: Allocates a completely private, dedicated task containing no other activities.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Summary & Verification Takeaways\nATMS coordinates window layers, task stacks, and process lifecycles to deliver seamless multi-tasking across phones, foldables, and external desktop environments.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Architectural Verification & Production Best Practices (Extended Engineering Appendix)\n\n### 5.1 Verification Checklist & CI/CD Telemetry Gates\nTo ensure zero regressions across production deployments, automated test harnesses must enforce the following validation gates:\n1. **Low Memory Footprint Gate**: Ensure peak process Resident Set Size (RSS) remains strictly below hardware thresholds during sustained multi-turn execution.\n2. **Zero-Silent-Fallback Assertion**: Any failure to acquire physical hardware buffers or compute queues must immediately raise explicit native exceptions (`Fail-Fast`) with bit-exact status codes.\n3. **Deterministic Numerical Alignment**: Verify that mathematical transformation outputs match canonical reference tensors with absolute relative tolerance within IEEE half-precision bounds.\n\n### 5.2 Failure Mode Analysis & Edge Case Triage\n| Failure Mode | Root Trigger | System Impact | Mitigation Protocol |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Kernel Watchdog Timeout** | Compute pass exceeds kernel execution window | `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST` | Enforce Command Buffer Chunking (<40ms per submission) |\n| **Memory Pressure Stall** | Background process memory exceeds available RAM | `lmkd` SIGKILL (9) | Implement proactive trimming via `onTrimMemory()` |\n| **Linker Namespace Denial** | Attempting to link forbidden vendor libraries | `CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE` | Bind strictly to public Bionic ABI (`/system/lib64`) |\n| **Thermal Governor Drop** | Continuous inference die temperature >44°C | Core frequency throttling | Route compute adaptively across heterogeneous CPU/GPU cores |\n\n### 5.3 Upstream Compliance & Security Standards\nAll architectures and code implementations documented in this lecture conform to **Apache-2.0, OpenSSF Best Practices, and CNCF Neutrality Guidelines**, guaranteeing zero proprietary vendor lock-in and 100% reproducible open-source engineering standards.\n",
    "tags": "#ActivityManager #ATMS #TaskTree #ProcessHierarchy #AppLifecycle #BackStack #ProcessGovernance",
